?rva006C39F0@Rva006C39F0Owner@@QAE_NIIIPAX@Z	0x006C39F0	191	partial	ARG ROLES CORRECTED, which is a real semantic fix the bank got backwards, and the register-allocation blocker is now the ONLY remaining defect. (1) ARG2 AND ARG3 WERE SWAPPED IN THE BANK. Tracing esp through the prologue puts the four stack arguments at fixed distances, and every reload then names exactly one of them: after push ecx/ebx/ebp/edi/esi esp = S0-20 so [esp+0x20]=S0+12=arg3 (mov esi,[esp+0x20] at 0x6C3A3C), [esp+0x1c]=S0+8=arg2 (mov edi,[esp+0x1c] at 0x6C3A48), [esp+0x18]=S0+4=arg1 (mov edi,[esp+0x18] at 0x6C3A6A); and before push edi, [esp+0x14]=S0+4=arg1 (mov edi,[esp+0x14] at 0x6C3A13, the hash key). So ARG2 is what SIZES the run -- the value tested to zero at 0x6C3A4C, pushed to 0x006C3940 at 0x6C3A54, and whose low word is written at both ends of the allocation -- and ARG3 is the insert length on the allocated path, reloaded into edi at 0x6C3A6A and pushed first to 0x006C21C0. The bank had arg2 as the allocated insert length and arg3 as the run size, which is inverted on both. ARG1 remains the direct-buffer insert length because the buffer!=0 branch at 0x6C3A46 reaches the shared insert at 0x6C3A70 without reloading edi, so edi is still the key from 0x6C3A13. (2) The do-while entry-test fix, the shared-exit  lifecycle (preset 1 / xor bl,bl / mov bl,1) and the -in-ecx spill are all preserved from the bank and still correct. MEASURED ON ONE HARNESS, LCS over the 191B target, cache cleared between variants: the unmodified bank emits 171B with LCS 132; the argument correction alone emits 171B / LCS 132; wrapping the whole body in if(m_tracking){...} with the shared  outside it lifts LCS to 143 at 175B (and it is the wrapper, not the arg fix alone, that pays -- the flat goto-done form with corrected args stays at 132); lifting the insert length into a ternary initialised from buffer, , lifts it to LCS 148 at 181B, which is what is banked here; and a hand-rolled  with a later  assignment inside the alloc branch stays at 143, so the ternary form specifically is load-bearing. STILL OPEN and now the single remaining defect: the CALLEE-SAVE ALLOCATION SCHEDULE. Retail emits push ebx / mov [esp+4],ecx / mov bl,1 / je, so ebx is the FIRST callee-save and the this-spill lands in the frame home push ebx has just vacated; ebp (+0x6), edi (+0x12) and esi (+0x3B) are then pushed IN THE BODY at their first use. This body hoists push ebp / push edi ahead of the ebx+spill, so the this-spill is displaced to [esp+0x10] and every later frame slot follows. Cause is that MSVC 7.1 allocates every callee-save at the point of maximum pressure across the whole function rather than at first use, and the tracking-off / key-found / insert-success / release / failure exits all converge on the shared , which keeps all four live from entry. MEASURED AND REJECTED this pass, all worse: /O1 emits 159B but switches to a real EBP frame and parks  at [ebp+0xb], never allocating ebx for it at all, so the prologue cannot match; /Ot and /O2 /Ob1 are byte-identical to /O2 at 171B / LCS 132; splitting the chain walk and the allocation into separate block scopes (175B, LCS 132); a bare  replacing the bool (189B, LCS 138, the worst of the block forms); duplicating the insert call into the direct and allocated arms (139B -- MSVC folds it away entirely); splitting the insert and its failure arm into two if/else bodies (124B, LCS 74, far worse); lifting  out of the alloc branch into  (184B, LCS 135, the lift is semantically wrong on the alloc-failure path); and a -local alias for  (175B, LCS 143, byte-identical to the bank). t=35min model=space-bunny-alpha blocker=callee-save-allocation-hoisted-to-prologue-so-this-spill-displaced-from-esp-plus-4-to-esp-plus-10 score=0.98 score=0.98 stash=reverse/attempts/0x006c39f0.cpp
